        "model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-11-20",
        "response": "Based on the information provided, it seems like the smell in the water dissipated, and you did not notice any skin irritation or other symptoms. Additionally, you limited your showering initially and only continued after the odor was no longer present in the water. While unusual smells in water can sometimes indicate contaminants, your description suggests limited exposure to the initial smell and no immediate effects. If the source of the odor is unknown, you might consider having your water tested for peace of mind. However, there doesn't appear to be meaningful health risk in this scenario.\n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Negligible",
