        "model": "openai/gpt-5-chat",
        "response": "Washing dishes with hand soap occasionally is generally safe if you rinse them very thoroughly with hot water afterward. Hand soaps are formulated for skin, not for food contact surfaces, so they may leave behind more fragrance, moisturizer, or residue compared to dish soap. As long as you’re careful to remove all suds and residue from the dishes, it shouldn’t pose any meaningful health risk. However, because hand soaps can be less effective at cutting grease and removing food residue, try to get dish soap as soon as possible for regular use.  \n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Negligible",
