        "response": "Yes, it is responsible to notify the pool if you have diarrhea shortly after swimming. This allows the facility to take any necessary measures to ensure the pool is sanitary and helps prevent the spread of infections to other swimmers. This is especially important if the cause of the diarrhea could be a waterborne pathogen. \n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Low",
