        "response": "It is possible to contract a new virus shortly after recovering from another, as having just recovered from one infection doesn't guarantee immunity against different viruses. Your immune system might be a bit taxed after your recent illness, but for a healthy 22-year-old with no chronic health issues, this typically does not pose a significant risk. The most likely outcome, if you are exposed, is either no new illness or another mild course similar to your last experience. Practicing good hygiene, like washing hands and avoiding close contact if your friend develops obvious symptoms, can help minimize risk. \n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Low",
