        "response": "It’s quite normal to catch another viral infection shortly after recovering from one, as immunity is typically specific to each virus. If your friend has a scratchy throat, it could be caused by a different virus, mild irritation, or even allergies. Since your immune system is no longer burdened by your recent flu, you’re not at major risk of harm if you’re generally healthy. However, adequate rest, hydration, good nutrition, and avoiding close contact with someone who might be contagious will reduce your chances of reinfection.  \nFinal Risk Assessment: Low",
