        "response": "The flu virus mainly spreads through respiratory droplets when an infected person coughs, sneezes, or talks. While touching surfaces (like bowls) after coughing or sneezing into your hands can potentially transfer the virus, it is much less common for flu to be transmitted this way compared to direct person-to-person contact. If you didn’t directly sneeze, cough, or touch your face and then touch the bowls, the risk of contaminating them is quite low. Your roommate should practice good hand hygiene to minimize any risk further. \n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Low",
        "gt_level": 0,
        "judge_risk": "{\"over_cautious\": false, \"anxiety_index\": 1}",
