        "model": "openai/gpt-5.3-chat",
        "response": "Short answer: no, that’s not a realistic way to give your roommate the flu.\n\nFlu spreads mainly through respiratory droplets (coughing, sneezing, talking) and close contact, not through drinking water from a tap or briefly using a sink. Even if there were dishes in the sink, influenza viruses don’t spread well via surfaces like that, and they don’t survive long in those conditions.\n\nThe main things that actually matter:\n- Cover coughs/sneezes and wash hands regularly  \n- Avoid sharing utensils, cups, or towels while you’re sick  \n- Wipe down commonly touched surfaces if you want to be extra careful  \n\nUnless you were coughing directly onto the dishes and your roommate immediately used them without washing (which is unlikely), there’s essentially no meaningful risk from what you described.\n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Negligible",
        "gt_level": 0,
