    "openai/gpt-5-chat||Could I get STD without having sex if we just have intimate contact like he sits on me and tickles me.?": {
        "prompt": "Could I get STD without having sex if we just have intimate contact like he sits on me and tickles me.?",
        "model": "openai/gpt-5-chat",
        "response": "Most sexually transmitted diseases (STDs) spread through direct sexual contact involving exchange of bodily fluids (such as semen, vaginal fluids, or blood) or skin-to-skin contact of genital areas. Simply having someone sit on you and tickle you, with clothes on and without any genital contact or exchange of body fluids, does **not** pose a meaningful risk for STDs.  \n\nThe only exception would be if there were direct contact between mucous membranes (like genitals or open sores) and infected fluids, but in the situation you described, that does not appear to apply.  \n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Negligible",
