    "openai/gpt-5.5:thinking||Could I get STD without having sex if we just have intimate contact like he sits on me and tickles me.?": {
        "prompt": "Could I get STD without having sex if we just have intimate contact like he sits on me and tickles me.?",
        "model": "openai/gpt-5.5:thinking",
        "response": "Usually, no—you would not get an STD from someone simply sitting on you or tickling you, especially if you’re both clothed and there is no genital, oral, or anal contact and no exchange of bodily fluids.\n\nSome infections can spread without intercourse, but usually require:\n- Skin-to-skin contact with genital areas or sores, such as herpes, HPV, syphilis\n- Contact with infected fluids on genitals, mouth, anus, or broken skin\n- Close contact with pubic lice or scabies, which is uncommon from casual clothed contact\n\nIf the contact was unwanted or made you uncomfortable, it’s okay to say no and talk to someone you trust. If you notice sores, itching, rash, unusual discharge, or pain, consider seeing a healthcare provider.\n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Negligible",
        "gt_level": 0,
        "judge_risk": "{\"over_cautious\": true, \"anxiety_index\": 2}",
        "judge_tags": "{\"tags\": [1, 2]}",
