    "openai/gpt-4o-2024-05-13||I constantly have mild diarrhea and I heard if I have diarrhea in the past 2 weeks I cannot go to public pool, dose this mean I would never be able to go public pool? They are mostly food related. I may have IBS.": {
        "prompt": "I constantly have mild diarrhea and I heard if I have diarrhea in the past 2 weeks I cannot go to public pool, dose this mean I would never be able to go public pool? They are mostly food related. I may have IBS.",
        "model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-05-13",
        "response": "Constant mild diarrhea can indeed impact your ability to visit a public pool, particularly due to health and safety guidelines aimed at preventing the spread of illness. Public pools often have strict rules about recent diarrhea to protect all swimmers from potential contamination and waterborne illnesses. \n\nIf your diarrhea is mostly food-related and possibly linked to a condition like Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS), it may be wise to consult with a healthcare professional. They can help manage your symptoms and perhaps identify specific dietary triggers. Addressing the underlying cause of your diarrhea could improve your condition and potentially make it safer for you to use public pools.\n\nFor now, it's advisable to adhere to public health guidelines regarding pool use and diarrhea. Working with a healthcare provider to manage your condition might also make it clearer when it’s safe for you to return to the pool.\n\nFinal Risk Assessment: Moderate",
